></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>NaBC1 is a ubiquitous electrogenic Na<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>-coupled borate transporter essential for cellular boron homeostasis and cell growth and proliferation.</article-title><source>Mol Cell Bio</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>331</fpage><lpage>341</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006009-Eckhert1"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eckhert</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Boron stimulates embryonic trout growth.</article-title><source>J Nutr</source><volume>128</volume><fpage>2488</fpage><lpage>2493</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9868197</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006009-Rowe1"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rowe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Eckhert</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Boron is required for zebrafish embryogenesis.</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Biology</source><volume>202</volume><fpage>1649</fpage><lpage>1654</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10333510</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006009-Barranco1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barranco</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Eckhert</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Boric acid inhibits prostate cancer cell proliferation.</article-title><source>Cancer Letters</source><volume>216</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>29</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15500945</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006009-Barr1"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author">